course: dictionary
lesson: 14659
title: Choosing the better word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Preferable means better or more suitable. If one choice is preferable to another, you would rather have or choose it. «Walking is preferable to running near the pool» means walking is the better, safer choice.
explain: Look at the word parts: prefer means to like one thing more than another. So preferable describes something worth preferring. «It is preferable to show your working» means that showing your working is the better thing to do in maths.
explain: Use the swap check from earlier. Put a word like better in the sentence: «Walking is better than running near the pool» still makes sense, so preferable means better here. Watch for the phrase «preferable to», because it tells you what the choice is being compared with.
fact: Preferable means better or more suitable, so you would rather have or choose it.
fact: «Preferable to» is a common phrase: X is preferable to Y means X is the better choice.
fact: «Far preferable» and «infinitely preferable» make the comparison stronger.
fact: «It is preferable to show your working» means it is the better choice to do this in school.
fact: Preferable comes from prefer, which means to like one thing more than another.
exercise: «Walking is preferable to running near the pool.» What does preferable mean? | Faster | Louder | *Better or more suitable
exercise: «It is preferable to show your working in maths.» Which phrase means the same? | It is never a good idea to show your working | Your working is the same as the answer | *It is better to show your working
exercise: «A quiet bus is preferable to a noisy one.» Find and copy the phrase that compares two things. | *preferable to | quiet bus | bus | noisy one
exercise: Maya says, «Reading a book is preferable to watching the screen all afternoon.» What does she mean? | Reading and watching are exactly the same | Watching the screen is always the best choice | *Reading a book is the better choice
test: «Staying dry is preferable to getting soaked on the walk home.» What does preferable mean here? | Quieter | Longer | *Better | Wetter
test: Ravi asks, «Is it preferable to sleep early before a test?» What is the answer? | *Yes, sleeping early is the better choice | Preferable means sleepy | No, it is never better to rest
exam: Which sentence uses preferable correctly? | Preferable is a large red bus | *Fresh air is preferable to smoky air | The preferable dog ran across the park
